# builtin-lower correctly skips Decl items (type/class/instance declarations) when
# building CoreDocument entries so that expression keys are contiguous (0-indexed even
# when Decl items appear before Expr items in the document).
#
# The source document has a top-level [type ...] declaration (SurfaceItem::Decl) followed
# by a dict expression (SurfaceItem::Expr). builtin-lower must not increment the key counter
# for the Decl item, so the single Expr item gets key "0", not "1".
#
# CoreDocument entry keys are internal to the Rust type and not accessible from tinct
# builtins, so we verify key contiguity indirectly:
#   1. builtin-doc-expressions counts only Expr items (not Decls): count must be 1.
#   2. builtin-lower succeeds and returns a CoreDocument (not an error).
#   3. builtin-eval on the same document returns the correct value {x: 42},
#      confirming the Expr item's content is reached and the Decl does not
#      contribute a spurious entry to the evaluation result.
#
# If the original bug (incrementing expr_idx for Decl items) were present, the
# CoreDocument would still have 1 entry but keyed "1" instead of "0". That specific
# failure is not detectable at the tinct level; the checks below verify the
# surrounding invariants that the fix maintains.
[call [fn [let]
  [src:     [builtin-str-bytes "[type Color Red Green Blue]\n[x: 42]"]]
  [parsed:  [builtin-parse src "test.llt"]]
  [desug:   [builtin-desugar parsed.program]]
  [docs:    [builtin-program-docs desug]]
  [doc0:    [builtin-dict-get 0 docs]]
  # Count only Expr items (Decl items must not be counted).
  [doc-exprs: [builtin-doc-expressions doc0]]
  [expr-count-ok: [builtin-eq-int [builtin-dict-length doc-exprs] 1]]
  [resolved: [builtin-resolve doc0 []]]
  [tc:      [builtin-make-type-ctx]]
  [typed:   [builtin-typecheck-doc resolved.doc tc]]
  [lowered: [builtin-lower typed.doc]]
  [lower-type-ok: [builtin-eq-string [builtin-type-of lowered] "CoreDocument"]]
  # Evaluate the document using new env-dict protocol: builtin-eval lowered env.
  # env is empty {} since the document only references its own bindings.
  [exports: [builtin-eval lowered []]]
  [x-val:   [builtin-dict-get "x" exports]]
  [eval-ok: [builtin-eq-int x-val 42]]
  [builtin-int-add [builtin-int-add expr-count-ok lower-type-ok] eval-ok]]]
=== out
Int(3)
